{"title":"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The largest fraction in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/5788a1f81039e2f3955a58f3a80f612d986687f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{5}, \\frac{1}{10}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"38\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4a6cc740d41b3550c6548a69aa8c3d53c5cad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{1}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"417\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find the fractions for all the fractions and then see which is largest:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb6ba2d7be3e47e5c10c262e0eece12b656fbf90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = 0.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1dbd489721f90e92d2b9c2d84dd59da673e430ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} = 0.\\overline{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c14c591d9822ef4a4f2679f12e9cf7ab093046f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5} = 0.20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14ced84f856cd1f8ed11276921c3920f76ddd8af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10} = 0.10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We can see that the largest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31befa4c9c94a6484b810a1e0348a65d7243c639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"62\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because all of the fractions are unit fractions (a fraction expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divided by a positive integer), the largest fraction must be the one with the smallest denominator. This would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31befa4c9c94a6484b810a1e0348a65d7243c639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"62\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&a